<p>I like it, upvoted.</p>
<p>Three things though.</p>
<p>First off, minor nitpick, in the crossed out part: "They are to be fully informed fully of it's effects and to alternate shifts sleeping and resetting SCP-498 until the failure is repaired". You used fully twice.</p>
<p>Secondly, I personally don't like the "demotion to D-class." D-class is for those on death row, not guards that don't follow procedure. I would just say they were simply demoted, or re-assigned, or fired and given amnesiacs. Something like that. Your call.</p>
<p>Third, I agree with teaflower, using their first names makes it sound like a children's book instead of an incident report. I would either use last names or give them number designations.</p>

