															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1472934"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1352364489 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Nov 2012 08:48</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1609815">
									

<p>First of all, I kept waiting in vain for the bit at the end of the incident log that explained <em>why</em> the two D-Class were fighting - was it caused by SCP-498 or its effects directly, or was it in issue with the D-Class Personnel themselves? In other words, was the incident caused by the actual SCP object, or was it a matter of making a poor choice with who would be assigned to the job? Just saying that they were fighting kind of falls flat without some sort of explanation; I mean, why would D-4113 have <em>not</em> wanted to follow the procedure if he knew what SCP-498 did?</p>
<p>Second, I thought the deal was that the Foundation is &quot;cold, not cruel&quot;; I'm beginning to think that my definition of &quot;cold&quot; and &quot;cruel&quot; are different from those of everyone else on this website. To me, &quot;cold&quot; means &quot;unwilling to make exceptions or be lenient based on simple human empathy&quot;, while &quot;cruel&quot; means &quot;unnecessarily hostile&quot;, &quot;going out of one's way to display a lack of empathy&quot;, or &quot;the <em>opposite</em> of empathetic&quot;. In other words, terminating a D-Class Personnel who earned commendation for preventing a catastrophe falls under the category of &quot;cruel&quot; as opposed to &quot;cold&quot;, at least in my books - it's nonsensical, and in some ways counterintuitive, as I'm sure reliable personnel are hard to come by for the Foundation. If this is a matter of a policy that has been in place since <em>after</em> the last time someone edited this article, then my bad, but it should probably still be fixed; if I'm mistaken in how &quot;cold&quot; and &quot;cruel&quot; are defined, please feel free to correct me in my beliefs.</p>

							</div>

								
					
